findings.what:
The 1.28 m dome is bound to the head bone and pitches with it:
- 17-41 deg in attacks and abilities;
- 73 deg in the ult crouch;
- a held 54 deg in recall.

The brief asks for the cap to stay level (3 deg or less) in run, idle and the casts. It allows the forward tip only in Shoulder In and an 8 deg back-tilt in the Shelter Dome lift.

The maul head (0.26 x 0.22 x 0.37 m) lands only about 0.7-0.8 m in front of the body. It sits at chest height in idle and never rises overhead in Shelter Dome. In the match, the auto-attack reads as the white disc nodding toward the target with a green trail, and the maul itself is not readable at impact.

findings.fix:
Author a VALE 'domefall_leap' clip and play it as the ult dash's present.anim, driven by dash progress:
- a crouch with the dome pulled down;
- an airborne hold with the maul level overhead;
- a two-footed mortar slam.

Add a per-effect arc to self-dashes (the sim already has dash.arc and EntityView.height) with a 0.8-1.0 m peak, the shadow staying on the floor. Hold the slam pose for about 0.25 s before the dome shell VFX, and flare the windows at the apex as the warning beat.

